##################################################################################
# Company:        NOVA SST
# Engineer:       Joao Reis Antunes
# 
# Create Date:    07/2026 (mm-yyyy)
# Module Name:    baseband.sgdc
# Project Name:   TREX1 Digital Baseband Chain
# Target Devices: Technology-independent (design-level clock/reset facts only, no cell-specific data)
# Description:    SpyGlass CDC/RDC constraint file: declares the single clock domain, the async active-low reset, and its 2-FF synchronizer for CDC/RDC sign-off.
# 
# Dependencies:   Companion to baseband.sdc -- clock period must stay numerically in sync between the two. Consumed by the SpyGlass CDC/RDC goals (cdc_setup_check, clock_reset_integrity, cdc_verify, rdc_verify_struct).
# 
##################################################################################

# =============================================================================
# File    : baseband.sgdc
# Design  : trex1_rx_frontend_top
#
# Clock/reset summary:
#   - 1 clock domain:  clk  (10 MHz / 100 ns, ASIC digital-synthesis target -
#     see baseband.sdc v9 sec 7. NOT the FPGA's 100 MHz: nexys_a7.xdc's
#     clock/IO definitions target fpga_merged_test_wrapper, not this
#     synthesis top, and are not reused here - same distinction baseband.sdc
#     already makes.)
#   - 1 reset domain:  rst_n (asynchronous active-low, direct top-level port)
#   - No MMCM/PLL/clock dividers/gated clocks in the design
#   - No inter-domain crossings expected
#
# =============================================================================

current_design trex1_rx_frontend_top

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Clock definition  (SGDC syntax: 'clock', not SDC 'create_clock')
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
clock -name clk -period 100.000 -edge 0.000 50.000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Reset definition  (SGDC syntax: bare signal name, no get_ports)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
reset -name rst_n -value 0
reset_synchronizer -name rst_n_sync -reset rst_n -clock clk -value 0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Clock-group relationships
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single-domain design - no clock groups needed.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. CDC exceptions / quasi-static signals
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Configuration inputs set before reset release and held constant.
# Uncomment if SpyGlass raises false CDC violations on these:
# quasi_static -name fcw             fcw
# quasi_static -name mode_sel        mode_sel
# quasi_static -name decimation_rate decimation_rate
# quasi_static -name adc_res_sel     adc_res_sel
# quasi_static -name str_kp          str_kp
# quasi_static -name str_ki          str_ki
